Taking a ready thread's process stops it but leaves it on its queue,
so the next turn would run a thread that has no process to run in;
a queue holds only ready threads.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread names a queue it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -278,7 +278,6 @@ void sched_unhost(struct cap *hosted)
     }
     t->state = THREAD_STOPPED;
     *hosted = (struct cap){ 0 };
-    thread_settle(t);
 }
 
 /* The thread that earns a unit first of those it earns, else NULL, so that a look at each unit meets it once. */
